values ('b7c8d9e0-1f2a-4c97-8d67-8e9f0a1b2c77', 'race-and-ethnicity', 'Race and Ethnicity', 'Students treat race and ethnicity as social, historical, political, and institutional formations rather than fixed biological facts. The course traces how law, slavery, settler colonialism, immigration, empire, census categories, and citizenship built racial meanings, then how categories are made, remade, contested, and compared. Topics cover intersectionality, prejudice and discrimination, institutional and structural racism, whiteness and racial ideology, group experiences, life-chance institutions, criminal justice, media and identity, anti-racism, and a research-based case study.');

